<p id="mwA6U">Contestant Greer Blitzer faced controversy shortly after the season premiere after tweets of her defending <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blackface" title="Blackface" id="mwA6Y">blackface</a> were uncovered, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Bachelor_and_race" title="The Bachelor and race" id="mwA6c">continuing the trend</a> of contestants with racist social media histories being cast in the franchise.<sup about="#mwt230" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-61" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-61"}}'><a href="#cite_note-61" id="mwA6g"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA6k"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA6o">[</span>58<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA6s">]</span></span></a></sup> On January 24, 2023, Blitzer issued an apology for her past behavior.<sup about="#mwt233" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-62" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-62"}}'><a href="#cite_note-62" id="mwA6w"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA60"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA64">[</span>59<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA68">]</span></span></a></sup></p> 

<p id="mwA7A">The incident was further addressed during the <i id="mwA7E">Women Tell All</i> special on March 14, 2023, with host <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jesse_Palmer" title="Jesse Palmer" id="mwA7I">Jesse Palmer</a> acknowledging the franchise's failings to adequately address serious topics such as racism in the past.<sup about="#mwt236" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-63" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-63"}}'><a href="#cite_note-63" id="mwA7M"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA7Q"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA7U">[</span>60<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA7Y">]</span></span></a></sup> Blitzer also confirmed that she was educating herself on the history of blackface and had met with Dr. Kira Banks, a psychologist and diversity consultant.<sup about="#mwt239" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-64" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-64"}}'><a href="#cite_note-64" id="mwA7c"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwA7g"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA7k">[</span>61<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwA7o">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

